description:
FILED s543a (Opus, 2026-11-16), found by the line-track flip's probe 1 (scratch/s543a/probes/p1-caller.pl, p1b.pl, p1d.pl in the s543a worktree).

Since s543a every lowered statement writes the location registers (`(p-line N)`, `(p-file ...)`; ir-spec 6.3b).  The COMPILE-PHASE code does not: a BEGIN / END / CHECK / INIT / UNITCHECK body and a file-level `use` are emitted by the v1 TEXT path (Pl/Parser.pm `_process_scheduled_block` + `_process_children`; the `use` arm's `(p-eval-always (p-detect-at N) (p-use ...))`), which emits no location form.  So:

PROBE (perl 5.40.3 vs PCL s543a tree; p1b.pl):
    1 use lib "lib";
    2 use Imp;                      # Imp::import prints (caller)[1,2]
    3 BEGIN { my @c = caller(0); print "begin-caller0: ", scalar(@c), "\n" }
    4 sub w { my @c = caller; print "w: $c[1]:$c[2]\n" }
    5 BEGIN {
    6   w();
    7 }
    8 END {
    9   w();
   10 }
   11 w();
  perl: import: main F:2 / begin-caller0: 11 / w: p1b.pl:6 / w: p1b.pl:11 / w: p1b.pl:9
  PCL : import: main -:0 / begin-caller0: 0  / w: -:0       / w: p1b.pl:11 / w: p1b.pl:11

  * an `import` reached by `use` sees `-` line 0 (perl: the use line) -- a croak in import (`"bad" is not exported by the M module ... at F line N`) names `- line 0`;
  * a caller() / runtime die in a BEGIN body: `-` line 0 (the line is right inside a nested v2-lowered block, e.g. an eval {} in the BEGIN);
  * an END body: the line of the main program's LAST statement (a wrong positive line: perl names the END body's line);
  * `caller(0)` in a BEGIN block returns the empty list (perl: 11 fields, sub `main::BEGIN`) -- the BEGIN is not a frame.

SHAPE OF A FIX (sized, not built): `_emit_detect_at($stmt)` is already the ONE call at the head of both compile-phase forms (the BEGIN's p-BEGIN and the use's p-eval-always); a sibling emitting `(p-file "F") (p-line N)` there when line-track is enabled (not in eval mode: a string eval keeps its (eval N) file), the same at the head of an END/CHECK/INIT lambda, plus one `(p-line N)` per statement inside a scheduled block's `_process_children` (an option of that loop, set only by `_process_scheduled_block`).  Cost: two forms per use/BEGIN, one per BEGIN/END statement -- compile phase only.  The emission bar of that change is "every use / scheduled block gains the forms, nothing else moves".

Before s543a the file named in a BEGIN could be WRONG (the first path interned took file id 0, e.g. Exporter.pm); s543a reserved id 0 for `-` (guard Pl/t/die-location-01.t row 7).
